# [ICCRG](../wg/iccrg.html)

## Summary

The Internet Congestion Control Research Group (ICCRG) held its session during IETF 127. The agenda included working group administration, an update on the Hackathon congestion control activities, and four technical presentations covering:
1. Frameworks for evaluating heterogeneous congestion control algorithm (CCA) interactions and relative harm.
2. Extending L4S (Low Latency, Low Loss, and Scalable throughput) service end-to-end across internet backbone and transit domains.
3. Passive measurement of residential access network congestion, flow sharing, and application-informed video pacing.
4. Implementing hardware-assisted TCP Segmentation Offload (TSO) pacing on network interface cards (NICs) to eliminate microbursts.

